            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Facilities for mechanical treatment of WEEE scrap</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="57aded3d-4d3f-3d65-b03a-7392ab36aef2">electronics</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="8a771560-73e7-3ce6-8b6b-3a8100f4de4e">waste treatment</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The data represent an example of a mechanical treatment line for WEEE – comprising an initial shredder, a magnetic separator and an Eddy-current separator, a second (smaller) shredder, followed again by a magnetic separator and an Eddy-current separator – all this linked by conveyor belts. Total weight data are taken from producer information of such machines and own assumptions. Composition, infrastructure and production efforts are based on own assumptions. The dataset represents a production line with a total weight of 35’000 kg. Update 2023: The bill of materials is assumed to remain the same, but the background datasets are updating using new ICT datasets.; Geography: This module relates to the global situation.; UUID: 4442b11b-d3bb-3168-8f20-178bb3b67c58</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
